Bugfix: Skip unchanged directories during `restore --overwrite if-changed`

`restore --overwrite if-changed` always re-applied the metadata of every
directory to the target, even when it already matched the snapshot. On copy
on write filesystems such as ZFS this needlessly dirtied all restored
directories on every run, which could noticeably grow incremental snapshots
and sends.

Restic now compares the metadata stored in the snapshot with the existing
directory and only updates it if something differs. Directories that are
already up to date are reported as skipped. Metadata changes that cannot be
applied by the current user, for example changing the owner of a directory
without the required privileges, now cause a warning instead of being
retried on every restore.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22170
